{"name":"Modestly Peach","hex":"#eea59d","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"modestly","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adverb","definitions":["In a modest manner; with humility.","To a small degree."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/modestly"},{"term":"peach","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any tree of species Prunus persica, native to China and now widely cultivated throughout temperate regions, having pink flowers and edible fruit.","Soft juicy stone fruit of the peach tree, having yellow flesh, downy, red-tinted yellow skin, and a deeply sculptured pit or stone containing a single seed."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of or pertaining to the color peach.","Particularly pleasing or agreeable."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/peach"}],"entries":[{"title":"Modesty","blocks":[{"text":"Modesty, sometimes known as demureness, is a mode of dress and deportment which intends to avoid the encouraging of sexual attraction in others. The word modesty comes from the Latin word modestus which means 'keeping within measure'."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2b/CaliforniaBeachc1905.jpg/330px-CaliforniaBeachc1905.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Modesty"},{"title":"Peach","blocks":[{"text":"The peach is a deciduous tree that bears edible juicy fruits with various characteristics. Most are simply called peaches, while the glossy-skinned, non-fuzzy varieties are called nectarines. Though from the same species, they are regarded commercially as different fruits."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/92/Illustration_Prunus_persica_clean_no_descr.jpg/330px-Illustration_Prunus_persica_clean_no_descr.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Peach"},{"title":"Peach (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Peach is a color that is named for the pale color of the interior flesh of the peach fruit. Like the color apricot, the color peach is paler than most actual peach fruits and seems to have been formulated primarily to create a pastel palette of colors for interior design."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Peach_(color)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/f/f6/1868-skirt-lengths-girl-ages-Harpers-Bazar.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 1x","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/f/f6/1868-skirt-lengths-girl-ages-Harpers-Bazar.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","alt":"1868 diagram from Harper's Bazaar showing proper girls' skirt lengths increasing as they grow up","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3A1868-skirt-lengths-girl-ages-Harpers-Bazar.gif"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bc/Orthodox_pilgrim.jpg/500px-Orthodox_pilgrim.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bc/Orthodox_pilgrim.jpg/1280px-Orthodox_pilgrim.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bc/Orthodox_pilgrim.jpg/500px-Orthodox_pilgrim.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Orthodox pilgrim in the Laure of Kyiv-Perchesk. Pilgrims have to wear modest clothes and women and girls must cover their hair when entering a church or monastery.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AOrthodox_pilgrim.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/38/Femmes-Amish.jpg/500px-Femmes-Amish.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/38/Femmes-Amish.jpg/1280px-Femmes-Amish.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm